"The area $A$ under the graph can be approximated using the formula\n\n$$\nA≈(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{⏞}{f(-3)+f(0)+f(3)}})\\cdot {{Δx}_{⏟}}_{\\text{width}}.\n$$\n\nLet's set up a table with the values of $f(x)$ at each point:\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $5$ | $-2$ | $k$ |\n\nNow, we obtain the following approximation for the area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈(5+(-2)+k)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =(k+3)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3k+9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we are given that $A$ must be $6$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3k+9 & =6 \\\\ 3k & =6-9 \\\\ k & =\\frac{-3}{3} \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302224 13194139534664 true] [17592186302223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302225 13194139534664 true] [17592186302223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302226 13194139534664 true] [17592186302223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302227 13194139534664 true] [17592186302223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302228 13194139534664 true] [17592186302223 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534664 true] [17592186302223 1041 "selection" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302223 1104 #edb/ref 17592186302227 13194139534664 true] [17592186302223 1110 #uuid "5e096b0e-5bcb-5eaf-aa9d-dda496241782" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302224 1034 "-5" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302224 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534664 true] [17592186302224 1111 #uuid "a65fd1f2-8e43-5248-ad7d-a2bb1f666ba2" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302225 1034 "1" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302225 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534664 true] [17592186302225 1111 #uuid "1512b76d-6e60-5ca1-a9ca-28cb5503d393" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302226 1034 "0" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534664 true] [17592186302226 1111 #uuid "93bfc5c2-c8ad-51a3-a48a-5fa66ab4385c" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302227 1034 "-1" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302227 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534664 true] [17592186302227 1111 #uuid "178e916e-a7d7-543a-9e0c-44733074d144" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302228 1034 "-2" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302228 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534664 true] [17592186302228 1111 #uuid "916f618b-4f27-523b-8c19-655323981f9c" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302229 1017 #edb/ref 17592186302230 13194139534664 true] [17592186302229 1089 "q-20314" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302229 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534664 true] [17592186302229 1100 "A boat travels downstream on a river. The table below gives the speed $v(t)$, in miles per hour, of the boat at certain moments during its journey.\n\n| $t\\text{ (hours)}$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $1$ | $1.3$ | $1.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v\\text{ (mi/hour) }$ | $32$ | $35$ | $40$ | $65$ | $80$ | $65$ |\n\n Use the right Riemann sum for $v(t)$ over $[0,1.5]$ with five subintervals to approximate the total distance traveled by the boat.\n\n*Hint: The distance traveled is given by the area under the speed-time graph.*" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302229 1113 #uuid "0777d3ec-036e-5efa-8bf3-2c5eb2fd8c2c" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302229 1145 "Let $A$ denote the area under the curve $y=v(t)$ over $[0,1.5].$ \nIn this case, we have $n=5$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the total distance traveled can be approximated as\n\n$$\nA≈v(0.3)Δ{t}_{1}+v(0.7)Δ{t}_{2}+v(1)Δ{t}_{3}+v(1.3)Δ{t}_{4}+v(1.5)Δ{t}_{5},\n$$\n\nwhere each $Δ{t}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $t$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\nΔ{t}_{i}={t}_{i}-{t}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $Δt$'s.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $1$ | $1.3$ | $1.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Δt$ | $-$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n| $v(t)$ | $-$ | $35$ | $40$ | $65$ | $80$ | $65$ |\n\nWe plug in the numbers to approximate the number of liters and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈35\\cdot 0.3+40\\cdot 0.4+65\\cdot 0.3+80\\cdot 0.3+65\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =10.5+16+19.5+24+13 \\\\  & =83.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total distance traveled by the boat. So, the distance is approximately $83\\,\\text{mi}.$" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302230 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302231 13194139534664 true] [17592186302230 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302232 13194139534664 true] [17592186302230 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302233 13194139534664 true] [17592186302230 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302234 13194139534664 true] [17592186302230 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302235 13194139534664 true] [17592186302230 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534664 true] [17592186302230 1041 "selection" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302230 1104 #edb/ref 17592186302232 13194139534664 true] [17592186302230 1110 #uuid "9e1c4c87-7bb4-596b-8a24-9b1e6d4504af" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302231 1034 "81\\,\\text{mi}" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302231 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534664 true] [17592186302231 1111 #uuid "d16ccd57-77d7-5a10-a3aa-3cefb3978f92" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302232 1034 "83\\,\\text{mi}" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302232 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534664 true] [17592186302232 1111 #uuid "c5d8070e-fd81-56b2-85f4-c3bb03d65fcb" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302233 1034 "80\\,\\text{mi}" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534664 true] [17592186302233 1111 #uuid "5ab14b54-b687-5384-8a33-dfa5004f9a7d" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302234 1034 "70\\,\\text{mi}" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302234 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534664 true] [17592186302234 1111 #uuid "41a29ffe-7dfb-5bc5-be5b-967098f8a016" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302235 1034 "75\\,\\text{mi}" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302235 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534664 true] [17592186302235 1111 #uuid "266b14c8-f0cc-5c6c-8ef6-ffc8679db6be" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302236 1017 #edb/ref 17592186302237 13194139534664 true] [17592186302236 1089 "q-346457" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302236 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534664 true] [17592186302236 1100 "The following table shows the values of a continuous function $f(x)$ over the interval $[10,16].$\n\n| $x$ | $10$ | $12$ | $13.5$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $7$ | $2$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nUse the right Riemann sum, with the three subintervals indicated by the data, to approximate the area $A$ under the curve $y=f(x)$ over the interval $[10,16].$ \n\n$A≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302236 1113 #uuid "8e4448e6-52c9-5987-8c18-bd04f202595b" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302236 1145 "In this case, we have $n=3$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the area is approximated as \n\n$$\nA≈f(12)Δ{x}_{1}+f(13.5)Δ{x}_{2}+f(16)Δ{x}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere each $Δ{x}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $x$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\nΔ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $Δx$'s.\n\n| $x$ | $10$ | $12$ | $13.5$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Δx$ | $-$ | $2$ | $1.5$ | $2.5$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $2$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nFinally, we plug in the numbers to approximate the area under the curve and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈2\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 1.5+3\\cdot 2.5 \\\\  & =4+6+7.5 \\\\  & =17.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302237 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302238 13194139534664 true] [17592186302237 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534664 true] [17592186302237 1041 "field-1" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302237 1104 #edb/ref 17592186302238 13194139534664 true] [17592186302237 1110 #uuid "12c8e0d9-90f6-5b40-a59f-da2b4bbba80a" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302238 1034 "17.5" 13194139534664 true] [17592186302238 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534664 true] [17592186302238 1111 #uuid "9a12b8fd-2cfd-5e38-9917-e9c17c62f461" 13194139534664 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-115698" 17592186302208 "q-115698/selection" 1